{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# The Perceptron Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: The Perceptron class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Perceptron:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_inputs, learning_rate=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.weights = [0.0] * n_inputs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bias = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = learning_rate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, inputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total = sum(w * x for w, x in zip(self.weights, inputs))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += self.bias"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 1 if total >= 0 else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, training_data, epochs=100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            errors = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for inputs, target in training_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                prediction = self.predict(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                error = target - prediction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if error != 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    errors += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    for i in range(len(self.weights)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        self.weights[i] += self.lr * error * inputs[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    self.bias += self.lr * error"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if errors == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                print(f\"Converged at epoch {epoch + 1}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                return"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"Did not converge after {epochs} epochs\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Train on logic gates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "and_data = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 0], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 1], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 0], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 1], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "or_data = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 0], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 1], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 0], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 1], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "not_data = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"=== AND Gate ===\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_and = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_and.train(and_data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, _ in and_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {p_and.predict(inputs)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n=== OR Gate ===\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_or = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_or.train(or_data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, _ in or_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {p_or.predict(inputs)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n=== NOT Gate ===\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_not = Perceptron(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_not.train(not_data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, _ in not_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {p_not.predict(inputs)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Watch XOR fail"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "xor_data = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 0], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([0, 1], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 0], 1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ([1, 1], 0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n=== XOR Gate (single perceptron) ===\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_xor = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "p_xor.train(xor_data, epochs=1000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, expected in xor_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = p_xor.predict(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    status = \"OK\" if result == expected else \"WRONG\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {result} (expected {expected}) {status}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "It will never converge. This is the hard proof that a single perceptron cannot learn XOR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Solve XOR with two layers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The trick: XOR = (x1 OR x2) AND NOT (x1 AND x2). Combine three perceptrons:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```mermaid"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph LR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1[\"x1\"] --> OR[\"OR neuron\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1 --> NAND[\"NAND neuron\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x2[\"x2\"] --> OR"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x2 --> NAND"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    OR --> AND[\"AND neuron\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    NAND --> AND"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    AND --> out[\"output\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def xor_network(x1, x2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    or_neuron = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    or_neuron.weights = [1.0, 1.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    or_neuron.bias = -0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    nand_neuron = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    nand_neuron.weights = [-1.0, -1.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    nand_neuron.bias = 1.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    and_neuron = Perceptron(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    and_neuron.weights = [1.0, 1.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    and_neuron.bias = -1.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hidden1 = or_neuron.predict([x1, x2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hidden2 = nand_neuron.predict([x1, x2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    output = and_neuron.predict([hidden1, hidden2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"\\n=== XOR Gate (multi-layer network) ===\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, expected in xor_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = xor_network(inputs[0], inputs[1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {result} (expected {expected})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "All four cases correct. Stacking perceptrons into layers creates decision boundaries that no single perceptron can produce."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Train a Two-Layer Network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Step 4 hand-wired the weights. That works for XOR, but not for real problems where you don't know the right weights in advance. The fix: replace the step function with sigmoid and learn the weights automatically through backpropagation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TwoLayerNetwork:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, learning_rate=0.5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        random.seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w_hidden = [[random.uniform(-1, 1), random.uniform(-1, 1)] for _ in range(2)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b_hidden = [random.uniform(-1, 1), random.uniform(-1, 1)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.w_output = [random.uniform(-1, 1), random.uniform(-1, 1)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b_output = random.uniform(-1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = learning_rate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def sigmoid(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = max(-500, min(500, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, inputs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.inputs = inputs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.hidden_outputs = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            z = sum(w * x for w, x in zip(self.w_hidden[i], inputs)) + self.b_hidden[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.hidden_outputs.append(self.sigmoid(z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z_out = sum(w * h for w, h in zip(self.w_output, self.hidden_outputs)) + self.b_output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.output = self.sigmoid(z_out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, training_data, epochs=10000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for epoch in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total_error = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for inputs, target in training_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                output = self.forward(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                error = target - output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total_error += error ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                d_output = error * output * (1 - output)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                saved_w_output = self.w_output[:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                hidden_deltas = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for i in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    h = self.hidden_outputs[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    hd = d_output * saved_w_output[i] * h * (1 - h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    hidden_deltas.append(hd)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for i in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    self.w_output[i] += self.lr * d_output * self.hidden_outputs[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.b_output += self.lr * d_output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for i in range(2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    for j in range(len(inputs)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        self.w_hidden[i][j] += self.lr * hidden_deltas[i] * inputs[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    self.b_hidden[i] += self.lr * hidden_deltas[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = TwoLayerNetwork(learning_rate=2.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net.train(xor_data, epochs=10000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for inputs, expected in xor_data:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = net.forward(inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    predicted = 1 if result >= 0.5 else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {inputs} -> {result:.4f} (rounded: {predicted}, expected {expected})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two key differences from Step 4. First, sigmoid replaces the step function -- it's smooth, so gradients exist. Second, the `train` method propagates error backward from output to hidden layer, adjusting every weight proportionally to its contribution to the error. That's backpropagation in 20 lines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is the bridge to Lesson 03. The math behind `d_output` and `hidden_deltas` is the chain rule applied to the network graph. We'll derive it properly there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Train a perceptron on a NAND gate (the universal gate - any logic circuit can be built from NAND). Verify its weights and bias form a valid decision boundary.\n2. Modify the Perceptron class to track the decision boundary (w1*x1 + w2*x2 + b = 0) at each epoch. Print how the line shifts during training on the AND gate.\n3. Build a 3-input perceptron that outputs 1 only when at least 2 of the 3 inputs are 1 (a majority vote function). Is this linearly separable? Why?"
      ]
    }
  ],
